1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,180
On screen, he is an eye.

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:06,310
A great eye of fire, burning
on top of a black tower,

3
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:07,550
watching everything.

4
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:10,130
But the books tell a very different story.

5
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:14,550
In the books, one of the wisest Elves
in Middle-earth says something strange

6
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,110
about him.

7
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:17,420
"For nothing is evil in the beginning.

8
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:21,490
Even Sauron was not so."
Before the Dark Lord,

9
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:24,670
before the Ring, before the
Eye, he had another name.

10
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:26,880
A name that meant admirable.

11
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:30,070
So who was Sauron, before he was evil?

12
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:40,070
In Rivendell, in the autumn, a council
gathers in the house of Elrond.

13
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:44,530
Elves, Dwarves, Men, two hobbits, and
a third hobbit hiding in the corner,

14
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:45,430
uninvited.

15
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:48,010
Frodo holds up a little ring of gold.

16
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:51,890
Plain, smooth, and the most dangerous
thing in the world.

17
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:56,470
A man of Gondor asks: why not
use it against the Enemy?

18
00:00:56,870 --> 00:00:58,300
And Elrond says no.

19
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:02,800
Whoever wields it will only
become the next Dark Lord.

20
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,190
"For nothing is evil in
the beginning," he says.

21
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:11,450
"Even Sauron was not so."
It is a single line,

22
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:13,170
and the story moves on.

23
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:15,750
But the books never forget it.

24
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:20,000
They tell us exactly how a spirit
of light became the Dark Lord.

25
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:25,060
And it begins long before
the Sun, in a forge.

26
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:30,150
Before the world was made,
there were spirits.

27
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:33,570
The greatest were the Valar,
the powers of the world.

28
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,410
Beneath them served the
Maiar: lesser spirits,

29
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,470
but mightier than any king.

30
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,830
One of the Valar was Aulë, the smith.

31
00:01:43,230 --> 00:01:45,800
He shaped the mountains and loved stone,

32
00:01:45,650 --> 00:01:47,380
and metal, and gems.

33
00:01:47,830 --> 00:01:50,680
He loved making things,
and he loved to teach.

34
00:01:51,510 --> 00:01:55,190
Among the Maiar of his
forge, one stood out.

35
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:58,530
The books say he was mighty in
the lore of Aulë's people,

36
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:00,370
and remained so to the end.

37
00:02:01,140 --> 00:02:03,430
In notes published long after the books,

38
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,530
we even learn his first name.

39
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:06,690
Mairon.

40
00:02:07,090 --> 00:02:09,740
In the elvish tongue, it
means the admirable.

41
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:10,880
And he was.

42
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:13,020
His gift was order.

43
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:17,510
He loved planning, and structure, and
things working as they were meant

44
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:17,770
to.

45
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,430
He disliked confusion, and waste.

46
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:21,950
It was his virtue.

47
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:26,310
And according to those same notes,
it was also the cause of his fall.

48
00:02:28,910 --> 00:02:31,360
Among the Valar, one would not wait.

49
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:35,860
Melkor, the mightiest of them all,
wanted to shape the world alone,

50
00:02:36,170 --> 00:02:37,580
quickly, and his way.

51
00:02:38,070 --> 00:02:39,460
The others worked slowly.

52
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:42,670
They debated, and waited,
and let things grow.

53
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:46,300
To a mind like Mairon's, it
must have looked like chaos.

54
00:02:46,990 --> 00:02:49,400
Melkor looked like a master
who got things done.

55
00:02:49,850 --> 00:02:53,440
That, the notes say, is what
first drew Mairon to him.

56
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:55,670
Not cruelty.

57
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:56,750
Efficiency.

58
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:59,570
In the beginning of the
world, the books say,

59
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:01,410
Melkor seduced him to his side.

60
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:06,140
The smith's apprentice left the light
and knelt before his new master in

61
00:03:05,990 --> 00:03:06,580
the dark.

62
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:10,400
Melkor became Morgoth, the
Black Foe of the World.

63
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:13,810
And Mairon was given a new name
by those who feared him.

64
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:14,710
Sauron.

65
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,410
The abhorred.

66
00:03:16,810 --> 00:03:20,020
The Grey Elves called him
Gorthaur the Cruel.

67
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:24,630
The books say he was less evil than
his master in only one way.

68
00:03:25,030 --> 00:03:27,860
For a long time, he served
another, and not himself.

69
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:32,530
If you want to see Middle-earth
the way it is in the books,

70
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,830
subscribe to the Mythic Archives.

71
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:40,310
Because the next part of this story takes
place on an island of werewolves.

72
00:03:43,510 --> 00:03:47,900
In the wars of the First Age, the Elves
held a white tower on an island

73
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:49,020
in the river Sirion.

74
00:03:49,610 --> 00:03:50,540
Sauron took it.

75
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:53,390
Fear went before him, and
the defenders fled.

76
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,410
The fair island became Tol-in-Gaurhoth,

77
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:58,090
the Isle of Werewolves.

78
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:02,270
The books now call him a sorcerer
of dreadful power,

79
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:06,650
master of shadows and of phantoms,
misshaping what he touched,

80
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,590
twisting what he ruled.

81
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:10,340
Lord of werewolves.

82
00:04:10,850 --> 00:04:13,220
But his truest weapon was the lie.

83
00:04:13,850 --> 00:04:18,500
He lured an outlaw named Gorlim with a
phantom of his wife's face at a lighted

84
00:04:18,350 --> 00:04:22,380
window, and promised to give her back
if Gorlim betrayed his leader.

85
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:24,140
Gorlim broke.

86
00:04:24,730 --> 00:04:27,140
Then Sauron told him she was already dead.

87
00:04:27,870 --> 00:04:31,740
One day, a band of Orcs passed the
tower without reporting to him.

88
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:33,480
Sauron had them seized.

89
00:04:33,930 --> 00:04:35,000
They were not Orcs.

90
00:04:35,450 --> 00:04:38,980
They were Finrod Felagund,
the golden-haired Elf-king,

91
00:04:39,230 --> 00:04:41,920
and a mortal man named Beren, in disguise.

92
00:04:41,770 --> 00:04:45,850
Finrod and Sauron fought, not with swords,

93
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,870
but with songs of power.

94
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:52,230
Sauron sang of piercing,
of opening, of treachery.

95
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:56,550
Finrod sang of secrets kept,
of the prison opening,

96
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:58,210
and the chain that snaps.

97
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,570
Sauron was stronger.

98
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:03,470
And Felagund fell before the throne.

99
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:08,040
The prisoners were thrown into a pit.

100
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:11,050
One by one, a wolf came
for them in the dark,

101
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:12,630
and not one betrayed the others.

102
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:17,850
When at last it came for Beren, the
Elf-king broke his chains and fought

103
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:19,010
it with his bare hands.

104
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:22,130
He saved his friend, and
it cost him his life.

105
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:25,350
Then, from the bridge, there came a song.

106
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:26,790
Lúthien had come.

107
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:29,730
Her robe was blue as the unclouded heaven,

108
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:34,690
her eyes grey as the starlit evening, her
hair dark as the shadows of twilight.

109
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:39,570
Beside her walked Huan, the
great hound of Valinor.

110
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:43,070
Sauron sent his wolves to the
bridge, one after another,

111
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:45,110
and Huan slew each one in silence.

112
00:05:45,940 --> 00:05:48,990
So Sauron went himself, in
the shape of a werewolf,

113
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:51,150
the greatest that had yet been.

114
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:55,690
Lúthien cast a fold of her
dark cloak before his eyes.

115
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:57,340
And Huan sprang.

116
00:05:58,250 --> 00:06:01,100
Wolf, serpent, his own true shape.

117
00:06:01,590 --> 00:06:04,140
Nothing Sauron became could
break the hound's hold.

118
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:08,250
At last he yielded, and gave Lúthien
the mastery of the tower.

119
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:13,110
He fled as a vampire, great as
a dark cloud across the moon.

120
00:06:15,710 --> 00:06:19,740
At the end of the First Age, the hosts
of the Valar came in their wrath.

121
00:06:20,470 --> 00:06:24,580
Morgoth's fortress was broken, and Morgoth
was thrust out of the world.

122
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:28,570
And Sauron did something no one
expects from the Dark Lord.

123
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:33,450
He put on his fair form again, bowed
before the herald of the Valar,

124
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:35,590
and renounced all his evil deeds.

125
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:40,790
The books add a remarkable line: some
hold that this was not falsely done.

126
00:06:41,190 --> 00:06:44,440
That Sauron truly repented,
if only out of fear.

127
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:48,830
The herald told him to go into the West
and face the judgement of the Valar.

128
00:06:49,230 --> 00:06:52,580
It might mean a long servitude,
to prove his good faith.

129
00:06:53,130 --> 00:06:55,220
And Sauron could not bear it.

130
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:58,090
Under Morgoth, his power had been great.

131
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:01,680
He was ashamed, and he would
not return in humiliation.

132
00:07:02,330 --> 00:07:05,660
So he hid himself in Middle-earth,
and fell back into evil,

133
00:07:05,910 --> 00:07:09,600
for the bonds Morgoth had laid
upon him were very strong.

134
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,970
This is the hinge of his whole story.

135
00:07:13,370 --> 00:07:14,500
Not hatred.

136
00:07:15,030 --> 00:07:15,540
Pride.

137
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:19,750
He told himself a story.

138
00:07:20,260 --> 00:07:22,230
The Valar had abandoned Middle-earth.

139
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:24,870
Someone had to heal it, and order it.

140
00:07:25,270 --> 00:07:26,100
Why not him?

141
00:07:26,710 --> 00:07:29,740
In the Second Age, a stranger
came to the Elves.

142
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:34,350
He was fair, and wise, and generous,
and he called himself Annatar,

143
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:35,730
the Lord of Gifts.

144
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:39,490
The High King, Gil-galad,
would not let him in.

145
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:42,830
But in Eregion, beside the walls of Moria,

146
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:44,890
the Elven-smiths welcomed him.

147
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:49,160
Their lord was Celebrimbor,
grandson of Fëanor,

148
00:07:49,530 --> 00:07:51,100
and they hungered for knowledge.

149
00:07:51,830 --> 00:07:52,960
Annatar taught them.

150
00:07:53,690 --> 00:07:56,900
And with his teaching, they
forged the Rings of Power.

151
00:07:57,570 --> 00:08:00,460
Then, in secret, in the Mountain of Fire,

152
00:08:00,670 --> 00:08:02,140
he made a ring of his own.

153
00:08:02,630 --> 00:08:05,140
One Ring, to rule all the others.

154
00:08:05,750 --> 00:08:09,060
Into it he poured a great
part of his own power.

155
00:08:09,590 --> 00:08:11,720
But the moment he set it on his finger,

156
00:08:12,050 --> 00:08:13,520
the Elves were aware of him.

157
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:17,270
They knew him, and saw that
he meant to master them.

158
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:20,940
In anger and fear, they
took off their rings.

159
00:08:21,370 --> 00:08:23,900
Three rings Celebrimbor had made alone,

160
00:08:23,750 --> 00:08:25,420
without Annatar's touch.

161
00:08:26,310 --> 00:08:28,760
Those, Sauron never found.

162
00:08:29,290 --> 00:08:34,560
He took Celebrimbor and tormented him,
and the lord of Eregion died without

163
00:08:34,410 --> 00:08:35,680
giving up the Three.

164
00:08:36,470 --> 00:08:41,740
On television, before Annatar, he wore
the face of a man called Halbrand,

165
00:08:41,850 --> 00:08:43,980
a lost king of the Southlands.

166
00:08:44,670 --> 00:08:46,400
Halbrand is the show's invention.

167
00:08:47,550 --> 00:08:52,620
In the books, Eregion knew only
one mask: the Lord of Gifts.

168
00:08:55,220 --> 00:08:59,730
Then came the Men of Númenor, the greatest
kingdom of Men that ever was.

169
00:09:00,130 --> 00:09:04,820
Their king, Ar-Pharazôn the Golden, landed
with such a host that Sauron's

170
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:05,620
armies fled.

171
00:09:06,270 --> 00:09:08,660
So Sauron humbled himself before the king,

172
00:09:08,510 --> 00:09:11,260
and let himself be carried across the sea.

173
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:12,480
A prisoner.

174
00:09:13,250 --> 00:09:15,840
Within three years, he was the
king's closest counsellor.

175
00:09:16,610 --> 00:09:19,000
He had the White Tree
of the kings cut down,

176
00:09:18,850 --> 00:09:22,200
and raised a great temple
to Melkor in its place.

177
00:09:23,090 --> 00:09:27,300
At last he persuaded the king to sail
against the Undying Lands themselves,

178
00:09:27,610 --> 00:09:29,960
to seize the life that never ends.

179
00:09:30,690 --> 00:09:32,300
And the world was changed.

180
00:09:32,750 --> 00:09:36,060
The sea opened, and Númenor
fell into the abyss.

181
00:09:36,950 --> 00:09:39,040
Sauron was in his temple
when it went down.

182
00:09:39,670 --> 00:09:43,880
His body was destroyed, and his spirit
fled back over the dark water to

183
00:09:43,730 --> 00:09:44,240
Mordor.

184
00:09:44,970 --> 00:09:47,750
But he had lost something forever.

185
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:53,250
The books say he could never again take
a form that seemed fair to Men.

186
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:56,320
And the later notes add one last detail.

187
00:09:56,870 --> 00:10:01,240
Until the downfall of Númenor,
he still called himself Mairon,

188
00:10:01,090 --> 00:10:02,420
the admirable.

189
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:05,470
After the drowning, the
admirable was gone.

190
00:10:08,070 --> 00:10:08,860
He rebuilt.

191
00:10:09,990 --> 00:10:13,100
When the Last Alliance of Elves
and Men besieged his tower,

192
00:10:13,610 --> 00:10:16,580
Sauron came out and fought Gil-galad
and Elendil himself,

193
00:10:16,850 --> 00:10:17,960
and both of them fell.

194
00:10:19,050 --> 00:10:21,460
Then Isildur cut the Ring from his hand.

195
00:10:22,570 --> 00:10:25,080
Isildur wrote that it was
hot as a burning coal,

196
00:10:24,930 --> 00:10:26,980
and that his hand was scorched.

197
00:10:27,550 --> 00:10:30,260
And here, the films and
the books part ways.

198
00:10:30,930 --> 00:10:34,080
On screen, the Eye is
the Dark Lord himself,

199
00:10:34,330 --> 00:10:36,660
a giant fire on top of his tower.

200
00:10:37,350 --> 00:10:40,900
In the books, the Lidless
Eye is his emblem,

201
00:10:41,270 --> 00:10:46,120
painted red on his soldiers' shields,
and the Eye rimmed with fire appears

202
00:10:45,970 --> 00:10:46,740
in visions.

203
00:10:47,450 --> 00:10:49,760
The books' Sauron has a body.

204
00:10:50,190 --> 00:10:53,520
In the Dead Marshes, Gollum,
who was tormented in Mordor,

205
00:10:53,550 --> 00:10:56,820
whispers to Frodo, "He has only
four on the Black Hand.

206
00:10:57,430 --> 00:11:00,600
But they are enough." Four fingers.

207
00:11:01,310 --> 00:11:04,800
Most readers believe the missing one
is the finger Isildur cut away,

208
00:11:05,130 --> 00:11:06,740
three thousand years before.

209
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:10,010
And when the Ring finally
falls into the fire,

210
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:13,130
a huge shape of shadow rises over Mordor,

211
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:16,710
crowned with lightning, and
stretches out a vast,

212
00:11:16,860 --> 00:11:17,910
threatening hand.

213
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:22,310
Then a great wind takes it,
and it is all blown away.

214
00:11:23,710 --> 00:11:27,140
So, who was Sauron, before he was evil?

215
00:11:27,950 --> 00:11:30,240
He was Mairon, the admirable.

216
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:36,250
A craftsman who loved order so much that
he forgot who the order was for.

217
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:41,850
He was offered one way back, and
his pride closed the door.

218
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:45,230
Nothing is evil in the beginning.

219
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:50,370
Could he have been saved, or was he
lost the first time he knelt in the

220
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:50,710
dark?

221
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:52,850
Tell us in the comments.

222
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,850
Like this video if the
books surprised you,

223
00:11:55,700 --> 00:12:00,390
and subscribe to the Mythic Archives for
the next record from Middle-earth.
